# Project Agent Workflow (Mandatory)

Follow this order for every task:

1. Read `.agent` first (architecture, module inventory, and scaffold rules).
2. Read applicable project rules.
3. Inspect the closest existing twin feature before editing (prefer Users or Roles).
4. Implement by matching existing project patterns — never invent a parallel structure.
5. Update `.agent` in the same session for every meaningful change.

## Mandatory Structure Patterns

### Backend (new CRUD resources)
- Model + migration under `app/Models` and `database/migrations`.
- Controller in `app/Http/Controllers/Api/` **must extend `BaseController`** and configure `$model`, `$searchableFields`, `$sortableFields`, `$relationships`, `$validationRules`.
- Override store/update only for domain-specific logic; keep trait JSON responses.
- Routes live in `routes/api/v1/<resource>.php` (Sanctum + permission middleware), then **import** via `Route::prefix(...)->group(base_path(...))` in `routes/api.php`.
- Add permissions in `RolePermissionSeeder` when introducing new gates.

### Frontend (new CRUD list resources)
- Types in `resources/js/src/types/<name>.ts`, re-export from `types/index.ts`.
- Service in `resources/js/src/services/<name>.ts` **must extend `BaseApi<T>`** and call `super("/<resource>")`.
- Page layout:
  - `pages/<name>/index.tsx`
  - `pages/<name>/components/<Name>Detail.tsx`
  - `pages/<name>/components/<Name>Form.tsx`
  - `pages/<name>/components/<Name>Modal.tsx` (wraps Form in `GenericModal`)
- Register lazy route + permissions in `router/routes.tsx`; update sidebar/i18n when needed.
- Reuse `DataTableWithSidebar`, `useSidebarDetail`, `useConfirmDialog`, React Query, sonner toasts.

### Exceptions
Only Auth, Organization profile, Logs (read-only), Settings mail, and Trash may deviate — see `.agent`. Do not treat deviations as a new default.

## Consistency Rules

- Keep structure and naming consistent with nearby files.
- Prefer minimal, focused edits over broad refactors.
- Do not introduce new patterns when an existing one already fits.
- Keep UI text/style aligned with existing screens unless asked to redesign.
- Preserve existing behavior unless user explicitly requests behavior changes.

## Completion Rules

- Run lints on edited files after substantive changes.
- Do not commit generated uploads or secret files.
- If a requested change conflicts with current architecture, ask before proceeding.
- Work is not complete until `.agent` reflects the new state (inventory + Change Log).
